# Trivy vulnerability ignore-list, read automatically from the repository
# root by `trivy fs .` and `trivy image`.
#
# TD-024 (see TECH_DEBT.md): rumqttc 0.25.1 (MQTT connector) hard-pins
# rustls-webpki = "^0.102.8", which carries these four advisories. The
# vulnerable code is unreachable from Arca: rumqttc only uses this copy of
# webpki for one error variant and never configures a CRL; MQTTS certificate
# validation actually runs through rustls 0.23.40 -> the already-patched
# rustls-webpki 0.103.13. No upstream fix exists yet. Re-assess if rumqttc
# ever starts configuring CRLs, or if a new rumqttc release relaxes the
# rustls-webpki requirement.
